# ADD OS — required environment variables.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development. `.env` and `.env.production` are
# gitignored and must never carry a real credential into the repository.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Enforced by `src/add-os/__tests__/no-secrets.spec.ts`, which fails the build if
# a committed env file contains a value that looks like a live credential.

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL of the ADD OS API. Production: https://core.add-sy.com (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).
# Baked in at build time — set it on the build machine, not on the server.
#
# There is NO fallback. `src/add-os/config/env.ts` throws at startup in a
# production build when this is unset, and warns loudly in development. An unset
# API base that quietly resolves to somebody else's host is an exfiltration path,
# not a typo — which is exactly what the Pinx placeholder `https://api.org` was.
VITE_API_URL=

# ── Optional: real-time reception updates ───────────────────────────────────
# Pusher Channels app key and cluster — the same values as ADD Core's
# PUSHER_APP_KEY / PUSHER_APP_CLUSTER (public; the secret stays on the API).
# With either unset, Arrivals / Active Sessions / Close Session poll every 30 s
# instead (src/add-os/services/realtime.ts). Baked in at build time.
# The notification bell uses the same connection, and polls every minute without it.
VITE_PUSHER_APP_KEY=
VITE_PUSHER_APP_CLUSTER=

# ── Optional: browser notifications (Firebase Cloud Messaging) ──────────────
# The Firebase project the member app already uses. Project settings → General
# → add a Web app for the four config values; Cloud Messaging → Web Push
# certificates → Generate key pair for the VAPID key. All public — a web app's
# Firebase config is visible to every visitor; the server key stays in ADD Core.
# With any of the five unset, the "enable browser notifications" button never
# shows and Firebase is never loaded (src/add-os/notifications/browserPush.ts).
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=

# ── Removed, deliberately ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_MAPTILER_API_KEY — GONE. Do not reintroduce.
#
# It arrived with the Pinx template carrying the template vendor's own live-looking
# keys (a different one in `.env` and `.env.production`). Its only reader was
# `src/components/maps/maplibre/Map.vue`, reachable solely from the unrouted demo
# page `src/views/Maps/MapLibre.vue` — so nothing in ADD OS ever used it, and
# `api.maptiler.com` never appeared in a build.
#
# `api.maptiler.com` is also unreachable from an isolated network by definition.
# If maps are ever needed, `maplibre-gl` is already a dependency and works against
# a self-hosted tile server — no third-party key, no external host.
